(From: Thomas Bergstrom <pharmacy@lakesidemedical.example>) Tj T*
(To: complaints@aivoapharma.example) Tj T*
(Date: Mon, 8 Sep 2026 09:14:22 -0500) Tj T*
(Subject: URGENT - Particles found in Ondansetron vials, batch OND25B119) Tj T*
T*
(Dear Quality Assurance team,) Tj T*
T*
(I am writing to formally raise a complaint on behalf of Lakeside Regional) Tj T*
(Medical Center regarding Ondansetron Injection USP 2 mg/mL, 2 mL single-dose) Tj T*
(vials, batch OND25B119, expiry 05/2028.) Tj T*
T*
(During routine pre-administration inspection this morning, our oncology nursing) Tj T*
(staff identified small floating particles in four vials from a carton of 25.) Tj T*
(The particles are translucent and fibre-like and are clearly visible when the) Tj T*
(vial is held against a black background under the inspection lamp. One of our) Tj T*
(pharmacists independently confirmed the observation.) Tj T*
T*
(No product from this carton has been administered to any patient. All 25 vials) Tj T*
(from the affected carton have been withdrawn from the ward and quarantined in) Tj T*
(our pharmacy under lock. The four affected vials are being held for return and) Tj T*
(we can ship them to you on request.) Tj T*
T*
(We received 200 vials of this batch on 12 August 2026 under purchase order) Tj T*
(LRM-PO-88214. The remaining stock is being held pending your response.) Tj T*
T*
(Given that this is an injectable product administered to oncology patients,) Tj T*
(we consider this extremely serious and request a response within 24 hours,) Tj T*
(including your assessment of whether other batches are affected.) Tj T*
T*
(Regards,) Tj T*
T*
(Thomas Bergstrom, PharmD) Tj T*
(Director of Pharmacy) Tj T*
(Lakeside Regional Medical Center) Tj T*
